## 1. Grant of License

Upon a verified purchase through the official Gumroad listing, the copyright
holder grants you a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, worldwide
license to use VAJRA according to the tier purchased:

### Core Tier (Free — MIT)

The core engine (MCP proxy, credential ring buffer, CLI, Rego policies) is
free under the MIT License — see `LICENSE-MIT`. Everything below applies to
the paid tiers.

### Starter Tier ($79)

You MAY:
- Use, run, modify, and deploy VAJRA for your own internal business purposes
  and for products or services you operate for your own customers — including
  AI agent credential brokering.
- Deploy unlimited instances for your own organization's use.
- Modify the source code freely; modifications are owned by you.

You may NOT:
- Redistribute, resell, sublicense, publish, or share the paid-tier source
  code (adapters, audit persistence, SSO template), in whole or in part, in
  original or modified form — including as a boilerplate, starter kit,
  template, scaffold, course material, or competing product.
- Offer VAJRA itself (or a derivative whose primary value is the VAJRA
  codebase) for sale or free distribution.
- Remove or obscure copyright, attribution, or license notices embedded in
  the source files.

### Pro Tier ($149)

Everything in Starter, plus:
- Full white-label rights: rebrand VAJRA, remove all VAJRA branding, and
  deliver it as part of your own commercial offerings to your clients,
  including agency/client agent projects and secure enterprise demos.
- Client deployments: install customized VAJRA instances on client-owned
  infrastructure (including air-gapped) as part of a paid engagement.
- Priority support.

You may still NOT redistribute the paid-tier source as a standalone
boilerplate, template, or product that competes with VAJRA.

